{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The enemy</b> — Ibn Labrat said: for he found חֵרְבוֹת with a kamatz in an ancient book, therefore he interpreted it as in חַרְבוֹת צוּרִים (Jeremiah 49:13). And what seems right to me: that the ḥet has ḥataf kamatz. And R. Moses said: it should have been אבד זכרם אתה, and likewise: יַעַן אֲשֶׁר גָּבַהְתָּ בְּקוֹמָה וַיִּתֶּן צַמֶּרֶת וְתִתֵּן צַמֶּרֶת — and he did not speak correctly, for the force of HaShem is in actions, as in מִפִּי עֶלְיוֹן לֹא תֵצֵא (Lamentations 3:38) — the meaning is the going forth of evil and good, and these are the decrees; and so too it is יַעַן אֲשֶׁר גָּבַהְתָּ בְּקוֹמָה וַיִּתֵּן גָּבְהָךְ. And in my opinion: האויב is like הַקָּהָל — חֻקָּה אַחַת לָכֶם (Numbers 9:14); and so the interpretation is: וְאַתָּה האויב — because the ruins that you destroyed to the end have come to an end, and cities you abandoned — אבד זכרם — you thought you would escape, and you forgot that HaShem sits forever and takes judgment from you; therefore after it: וַיהוה לְעוֹלָם יֵשֵׁב — and behold it is connected with אבד זכרם: the cities — behold HaShem has wiped out his name, as written above; and that is the meaning: He paid you back according to your deeds."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Resolved 'אמר בן לברט' as 'Ibn Labrat' following the standard identification; the reading 'בן לברט' appears to mean 'son of Labrat,' possibly a patronymic rather than a surname, but the referent is uncertain. The phrase 'החי\"ת חטוף בקמץ' literally means 'the ḥet is snatched with a kamatz,' i.e., has a ḥataf (hatef) kamatz; translated as technical grammatical terminology per voice rules. The final clause 'והוא הטעם שגמל לך כמעשיך' may be read as a summary statement, but its syntactic connection to the preceding argument is loose in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:54.970195498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}